## 🔥 SCENARIO 3: Detect CrashLoopBackOff for Pods

### ✅ What are we detecting?

When a pod **keeps restarting repeatedly**, it's likely in **CrashLoopBackOff**. You detect this by watching for **a non-zero rate of restarts over time**.

---

## ✅ PROMETHEUS ALERT QUERY

```prometheus
rate(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total{
  cluster_name="azure-eastus-st-085-np-aks-001",
  namespace="storefront-storefront-ut",
  pod=~"storefront-api-ut-.*"
}[10m]) > 0.001
```

> This means:
> **“At least 1 restart every \~10 minutes”**
> You can tune the `> 0.001` threshold for stricter sensitivity (e.g., use `> 0.003` for \~2 restarts in 10 minutes).

